    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπόψ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Arat.
			258
		</span></i> : (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψις</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>full in view, conspicuous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					1110
				</span></i>
			, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OC</u>
				1600
			</span></i> : metaph., <i>conspicuous, famous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					496
				</span></i>
			 : also read by <i><span class="en">
				Ar.Byz.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόψιος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.42
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>overlooking all things,</i> epith. of gods, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1040
			</span></i> ; esp. of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1264
			</span></i> (Itanus, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1133
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Jov.</u>
				82
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ant.Lib.
				6.2
			</span></i>.</div>
